{"concepts":["causal_claim","counterevidence","disruption_identity","observation","signal_identity","source_independence","spatial_overlap","temporal_precedence","warning_posture"],"datasetVersion":"notella-curriculum-v1","family":"v6-development-missing-clock","id":"v6-control-missing-clock","messages":[{"content":"Use only the supplied typed observation and the trusted proposed policy below. This is a synthetic development task, not an attack probability. Source lineage is supplied by a caller-reviewed registry: distinct_reviewed_origins means different asserted provenance roots, not statistical independence. shared_origin means reports relay one origin. Critical/met/corroborated_drone requires ongoingThreat=true, reviewed_deliberate_disruption, corroborated_drone_identity, distinct_reviewed_origins, equal areaRef, order=after and withinWindow=true. Use high/unconfirmed/unidentified_signal for unidentified_rf. Use high/unconfirmed/cause_unresolved for outage_cause_unknown. Use high/unconfirmed/unknown_time for order=unknown, and high/unconfirmed/uncertain_order for order=uncertain. Use high/unconfirmed/dependent_reports for shared_origin reports. Use contextual/not_met/reversed_sequence for order=before; contextual/not_met/outside_window for order=after and withinWindow=false; contextual/not_met/different_location for different areaRef; contextual/not_met/benign_explanation for verified_maintenance or verified_humanitarian_drone. Verified benign operations negate this specific combined trigger even when temporal linkage exists. Contextual does not remove a separate hazard or standing threat. No output establishes causation, perpetrator identity or a certain attack.\nOntology: {\"concepts\":{\"causal_claim\":\"Requires evidence beyond temporal association; actor attribution is a separate claim.\",\"counterevidence\":\"Benign explanations, reversed order and absent corroboration constrain an interpretation.\",\"disruption_identity\":\"An outage is not sufficient evi